* member.raceCode 0..1 PIQICodeableConcept "The race of the member." "Concepts classifying the person into a named category of humans sharing common history, traits, geographical origin or nationality.  The race codes used to represent these concepts are based upon the [Race & Ethnicity - CDC (CDCREC)](https://phinvads.cdc.gov/vads/ViewCodeSystem.action?id=2.16.840.1.113883.6.238) code system. Detailed race concepts are grouped by and pre-mapped to the 5 OMB race categories:

   - American Indian or Alaska Native
   - Asian
   - Black or African American
   - Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander
   - White."
* member.raceCode ^label = "Race Code"
* member.raceCode from http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.4.642.2.575 (required)
* member.ethnicity 0..1 PIQICodeableConcept "The ethnicity of the member." "Concepts classifying the person into a named category of humans sharing common history, traits, geographical origin or nationality.  The ethnicity codes used to represent these concepts are based upon the [Race & Ethnicity - CDC (CDCREC)](https://phinvads.cdc.gov/vads/ViewCodeSystem.action?id=2.16.840.1.113883.6.238) code system. Detailed ethnicity concepts are grouped by and pre-mapped to the 2 OMB ethnicity categories:

   - Hispanic or Latino
   - Not Hispanic or Latino."
* member.ethnicity ^label = "Ethnicity"
* member.ethnicity from http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.4.642.40.2.48.3 (required)
* member.city 0..1 string "The city for the member's primary address" "The name of the city, town, suburb, village or other community or delivery center."
* member.city ^label = "City"
* member.county 0..1 string "125	County	The county for the member's primary address." "The name of the administrative area (county)."
* member.county ^label = "County"
* member.state 0..1 string "The state for the member's primary address." "Sub-unit of a country with limited sovereignty in a federally organized country. A code may be used if codes are in common use (e.g. US 2 letter state codes)."
* member.state ^label = "State"
* member.state from http://terminology.hl7.org/ValueSet/USPS-State (extensible)
* member.country 0..1 string "The country for the member's primary address." "Country - a nation as commonly understood or generally accepted."
* member.country ^label = "Country"
* member.postalCode 0..1 string "This represents the member's 5 digit zip code." "A postal code designating a region defined by the postal service."
* member.postalCode ^label = "Postal Code"
* member.addressStartDate 0..1 string "Member address start date" "The date the address started to be in use."
* member.addressStartDate ^label = "Address start date"
* member.addressEndDate 0..1 string "member address end date" "The date the address stopped being in use."
* member.addressEndDate ^label = "Address end date"
* member.telecomSystem 0..1 PIQICodeableConcept "Telecommunications form for contact point." "Telecommunications form for contact point - what communications system is required to make use of the contact."
* member.telecomSystem ^label = "member telecom system"
* member.telecomSystem from http://hl7.org/fhir/ValueSet/contact-point-system (required)
* member.telecomUse 0..1 PIQICodeableConcept "Purpose of this contact point - home, mobile, work, etc" "Identifies the purpose for the contact point."
* member.telecomUse ^label = "telecom use"
* member.telecomUse from http://hl7.org/fhir/ValueSet/contact-point-use (required)
* member.streetAddress 0..1 string "Street name, number, direction & P.O. Box etc." "This component contains the house number, apartment number, street name, street direction,  P.O. Box number, delivery hints, and similar address information."
* member.streetAddress ^label = "Street address"
* member.primaryLanguage 0..1 PIQICodeableConcept "A language which may be used to communicate with the patient about his or her health" "The language which can be used to communicate with the patient about his or her health. Coded using a language code from BCP-47 (e.g. \"en\" for English, or \"en-US\" for American English)."
* member.primaryLanguage ^label = "primary language"
* member.primaryLanguage from http://terminology.hl7.org/ValueSet/Languages (extensible)

